{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CfLsdFLjLMsU6v3TjGxWC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So `!picker.isOpen` is false, meaning the picker is still open. The toggle event fires but `matches(':popover-open')` might return true (the popover was shown but the test dispatch doesn't close it). The issue is: in the test, the popover might actually be open via `showPopover()`, and dispatching a toggle event doesn't change the browser's popover state.\n\nI need to rethink the toggle handler. The `toggle` event on a popover has `newState` and `oldState` properties. Let me use those instead:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":75421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0b9f0b-1dc8-4717-a724-0e8ed0d9f10e","uuid":"86aace43-7eb6-4dac-88d4-848f6aa110b7","timestamp":"2026-09-23T18:50:42.079Z","request_id":"req_011CfLsdEtgnNeuWGA6KhkhE"}
