{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NZDrL2UfE9JiSsWPyMCwfx","type":"tool_result","content":"38\t- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n39\t  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n40\t\n41\t## Placement helper\n42\t\n43\t- `src/placement.ts` is a pure function shared by the autocomplete and\n44\t  picker for positioning popovers relative to an anchor. It must not\n45\t  reference `document` or `window` at import time so it stays safe for\n46\t  Node imports.\n47\t- Unit tests for placement live in `test/placement.ts` and run in Node\n48\t  via esbuild bundling (no browser needed).\n49\t- `renderTabs()` and `renderTones()` replace all children, so any DOM\n50\t  reference grabbed before a click or keydown that triggers re-rendering\n51\t  will be stale. Re-query after the action.\n52\t- Synthetic `KeyboardEvent` dispatches do not trigger native button click\n53\t  behavior in test harnesses. Grid cell Enter/Space must be forwarded to\n54\t  `click()` in the keydown handler; tab and radio Enter/Space rely on\n55\t  the test calling `.click()` after `keydown()` to simulate native\n56\t  behavior.\n57\t- The host `onKeydown` dispatches by `event.target`: grid cells, search\n58\t  input, tabs, and tone radios each have separate handlers. New keyboard\n59\t  controls should follow this dispatch pattern.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0b9f0b-1dc8-4717-a724-0e8ed0d9f10e","uuid":"475b8811-25dd-4368-9777-975b4c782a3d","timestamp":"2026-09-23T18:51:45.731Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-05-light-dismiss-and-focus-restoration/AGENTS.md","content":"- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n\n## Placement helper\n\n- `src/placement.ts` is a pure function shared by the autocomplete and\n  picker for positioning popovers relative to an anchor. It must not\n  reference `document` or `window` at import time so it stays safe for\n  Node imports.\n- Unit tests for placement live in `test/placement.ts` and run in Node\n  via esbuild bundling (no browser needed).\n- `renderTabs()` and `renderTones()` replace all children, so any DOM\n  reference grabbed before a click or keydown that triggers re-rendering\n  will be stale. Re-query after the action.\n- Synthetic `KeyboardEvent` dispatches do not trigger native button click\n  behavior in test harnesses. Grid cell Enter/Space must be forwarded to\n  `click()` in the keydown handler; tab and radio Enter/Space rely on\n  the test calling `.click()` after `keydown()` to simulate native\n  behavior.\n- The host `onKeydown` dispatches by `event.target`: grid cells, search\n  input, tabs, and tone radios each have separate handlers. New keyboard\n  controls should follow this dispatch pattern.\n","numLines":23,"startLine":38,"totalLines":60}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CfLsiTwerwPjGSA2kY3Jy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WDiGX3Q63JWQJ59LGpVtCs","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-05-light-dismiss-and-focus-restoration/AGENTS.md","old_string":"## Placement helper","new_string":"## Picker dismissal and focus\n\n- The panel uses `popover=\"auto\"` (not `\"manual\"`) when not inline.\n  Light dismiss and Escape are handled by the platform; no document\n  click listener is needed.\n- The `toggle` event on the panel keeps the `opened` flag in sync.\n  Use `ToggleEvent` with `newState:'closed'` to detect dismissal.\n- Focus restoration only happens when focus is inside the panel at the\n  time of close. Light dismiss and `disconnectedCallback` never call\n  `focus()`.\n- `EmojiButton` checks `typeof target.open === 'function'` instead of\n  comparing `localName`, so pickers registered under custom tags work.\n\n## Placement helper"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":525,"cache_read_input_tokens":79393,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":525},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0b9f0b-1dc8-4717-a724-0e8ed0d9f10e","uuid":"c7f8f32c-c9d2-4acd-a114-0e2b7483ea3f","timestamp":"2026-09-23T18:51:52.694Z","request_id":"req_011CfLsiTUcmfiXgYrM5dwZR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WDiGX3Q63JWQJ59LGpVtCs":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-05-light-dismiss-and-focus-restoration/AGENTS.md","old_string":"## Placement helper","new_string":"## Picker dismissal and focus\n\n- The panel uses `popover=\"auto\"` (not `\"manual\"`) when not inline.\n  Light dismiss and Escape are handled by the platform; no document\n  click listener is needed.\n- The `toggle` event on the panel keeps the `opened` flag in sync.\n  Use `ToggleEvent` with `newState:'closed'` to detect dismissal.\n- Focus restoration only happens when focus is inside the panel at the\n  time of close. Light dismiss and `disconnectedCallback` never call\n  `focus()`.\n- `EmojiButton` checks `typeof target.open === 'function'` instead of\n  comparing `localName`, so pickers registered under custom tags work.\n\n## Placement helper"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WDiGX3Q63JWQJ59LGpVtCs","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-05-light-dismiss-and-focus-restoration/AGENTS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b0b9f0b-1dc8-4717-a724-0e8ed0d9f10e","uuid":"de1cd98b-3895-464f-a1bd-593af864f718","timestamp":"2026-09-23T18:51:52.754Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-05-light-dismiss-and-focus-restoration/AGENTS.md","oldString":"## Placement helper","newString":"## Picker dismissal and focus\n\n- The panel uses `popover=\"auto\"` (not `\"manual\"`) when not inline.\n  Light dismiss and Escape are handled by the platform; no document\n  click listener is needed.\n- The `toggle` event on the panel keeps the `opened` flag in sync.\n  Use `ToggleEvent` with `newState:'closed'` to detect dismissal.\n- Focus restoration only happens when focus is inside the panel at the\n  time of close. Light dismiss and `disconnectedCallback` never call\n  `focus()`.\n- `EmojiButton` checks `typeof target.open === 'function'` instead of\n  comparing `localName`, so pickers registered under custom tags work.\n\n## Placement helper","originalFile":"# Working notes\n\n## Emoji data and search\n\n- `src/data.ts` is the adapter boundary for the Emoji Mart JSON dataset.\n  Keep the public `EmojiEntry` fields compatible with custom emoji data.\n- `src/search.ts` owns the shared ranking order: name prefix, name\n  substring, then keyword prefix.\n- The JSON dataset import uses `with { type: 'json' }`. The tsconfig\n  module must be `ESNext` (or `NodeNext`/`Preserve`) to accept import\n  attributes. esbuild preserves the attribute in ESM output and lowers\n  it to `require` in CJS output.\n- Changes to the data adapter should be checked with `npm run lint`,\n  `npx tsc --noEmit --project tsconfig.json`, and the browser test bundle.\n\n## Picker component conventions\n\n- Picker DOM stays light-DOM; its styles are injected once per document or\n  shadow root through `adoptedStyleSheets`.\n- Picker UI tokens use the `--emoji-picker-*` namespace so host styles can\n  theme the panel without relying on internal class names.\n- Picker category filtering should consume `EmojiEntry.category` or\n  `EmojiEntry.categories`, while text filtering should use `src/search.ts`.\n\n## Component exports\n\n- Public custom elements should register from their component module and keep\n  their DOM in light DOM with styles injected through adopted stylesheets.\n- Adding a public component requires updating the main entrypoint and its\n  explicit package subpath together so ESM and CommonJS builds agree.\n- `test/smoke.mjs` runs in Node after build and before the browser bundle.\n  It verifies ESM and CJS loading of every subpath. Extend it when adding\n  new subpaths or CSS export entries.\n## Picker state and interaction\n\n- Persisted picker preferences should use configurable attributes and guard\n  every `localStorage` read and write with an in-memory fallback.\n- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n\n## Placement helper\n\n- `src/placement.ts` is a pure function shared by the autocomplete and\n  picker for positioning popovers relative to an anchor. It must not\n  reference `document` or `window` at import time so it stays safe for\n  Node imports.\n- Unit tests for placement live in `test/placement.ts` and run in Node\n  via esbuild bundling (no browser needed).\n- `renderTabs()` and `renderTones()` replace all children, so any DOM\n  reference grabbed before a click or keydown that triggers re-rendering\n  will be stale. Re-query after the action.\n- Synthetic `KeyboardEvent` dispatches do not trigger native button click\n  behavior in test harnesses. Grid cell Enter/Space must be forwarded to\n  `click()` in the keydown handler; tab and radio Enter/Space rely on\n  the test calling `.click()` after `keydown()` to simulate native\n  behavior.\n- The host `onKeydown` dispatches by `event.target`: grid cells, search\n  input, tabs, and tone radios each have separate handlers. New keyboard\n  controls should follow this dispatch pattern.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":38,"oldLines":6,"newStart":38,"newLines":19,"lines":[" - Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,","   `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields."," ","+## Picker dismissal and focus","+","+- The panel uses `popover=\"auto\"` (not `\"manual\"`) when not inline.","+  Light dismiss and Escape are handled by the platform; no document","+  click listener is needed.","+- The `toggle` event on the panel keeps the `opened` flag in sync.","+  Use `ToggleEvent` with `newState:'closed'` to detect dismissal.","+- Focus restoration only happens when focus is inside the panel at the","+  time of close. Light dismiss and `disconnectedCallback` never call","+  `focus()`.","+- `EmojiButton` checks `typeof target.open === 'function'` instead of","+  comparing `localName`, so pickers registered under custom tags work.","+"," ## Placement helper"," "," - `src/placement.ts` is a pure function shared by the autocomplete and"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
